## Data flow

1. A client calls `POST /runs/wait` or `POST /runs/stream` (or `python -m {{package}} chat`).
2. `runtime/runner.py` starts a run with the limits from `settings.py` and hands the messages
   to the {{framework}} agent in `agent.py`.
3. The agent calls the model. Each tool call goes through `runtime/tools.py`, which validates
   the arguments against the generated model in `runtime/tool_args.py`, applies the approval
   policy, enforces the tool timeout and calls `tools/<name>.py`.
4. A tool that needs approval pauses the run (`status: interrupted`) until
   `POST /runs/{id}/resume` approves, edits or denies it.
5. Errors and invalid arguments go back to the model as tool results; limit breaches and
   timeouts end the run with `limit_exceeded` or `timeout`.
6. The final answer{{#if structured_output.enabled}} is validated against the output schema and{{/if}} is returned with the tool calls,
   usage and spans in the run record (`GET /runs/{id}`).

Run limits: {{limits.max_steps}} model calls, {{limits.max_tool_calls}} tool calls, {{limits.max_tokens}} tokens, ${{limits.max_cost_usd}}, {{limits.timeout_s}} s.

